      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.42,
      "end_seconds": 258.34,
      "duration_seconds": 26.92,
      "text": "right, here's what I'm thinking. I'm honestly not certain yet. It could be possible bacterial meningitis, or it might be meningococcal septicaemia. I'll request blood cultures, it'll help with possible meningitis. I think a lumbar puncture makes sense here, for possible meningitis. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.41,
      "end_seconds": 276.08,
      "duration_seconds": 16.67,
      "text": "I'm prescribing benzylpenicillin, 1.2 grams, once now, single dose. That should help with possible meningitis. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Call an ambulance now, this is an emergency"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
